1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,240
Listen to a talk in a history class.

2
00:00:03,240 --> 00:00:09,260
The Silk Road is an ancient trade route that connected the east and west.

3
00:00:09,260 --> 00:00:12,172
The Silk Road was not a single path,

4
00:00:12,172 --> 00:00:19,086
but a network of trade routes that spanned thousands of miles going through the modern day countries of China,

5
00:00:19,086 --> 00:00:21,270
and India, and further into Europe.

6
00:00:21,270 --> 00:00:26,140
It played a crucial role in the development of the civilizations it connected.

7
00:00:26,140 --> 00:00:32,009
It facilitated not only trade, but also cultural exchange and the spread of ideas.

8
00:00:32,009 --> 00:00:36,600
Merchants on the Silk Road traded a wide variety of goods from silk

9
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:39,210
and spices to precious metals and artwork.

10
00:00:39,210 --> 00:00:42,919
The route was named after the lucrative trade in silk fabric,

11
00:00:42,919 --> 00:00:46,290
which was one of the most sought-after commodities from China.

12
00:00:46,290 --> 00:00:51,150
However, it's important to note that the exchange was not limited to physical goods.

13
00:00:51,150 --> 00:00:55,030
It also included knowledge, technology, and religion.

14
00:00:55,030 --> 00:01:01,140
For example, Buddhism spread from India to China partly through interactions along the Silk Road.

15
00:01:01,140 --> 00:01:04,940
The cities along the route, such as Samarkand and Baghdad

16
00:01:05,160 --> 00:01:07,270
became prosperous centers of commerce and learning.

17
00:01:07,270 --> 00:01:12,090
They were melting pots of different cultures, languages, and traditions.

18
00:01:12,090 --> 00:01:17,170
Next, we'll explore the impact of the Silk Road on the economic development of Europe.
